        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119208,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Bone marrow and peripheral blood are always involved.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119209,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Patients present with clinical features similar to those of other acute leukaemias, typically secondary to cytopenias.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119210,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>There are too few reported cases to determine epidemiological patterns of this leukaemia. It has been reported in children and adults {34540694}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119211,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119212,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The pathogenesis of ALAL-NOS is largely unknown. Emerging data suggest that mutations in epigenetic regulators, as well as in components of the RAS and NOTCH pathways, may play a role {34540694; 34934076}. A recent study identified the presence of double <em>RUNX1</em> mutations in ALAL {34540694}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119213,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119214,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "<p>Blasts in the blood and bone marrow are usually immature and have no morphological features of differentiation.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Immunophenotype</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>Blasts do not express lineage-specific markers but rather combinations of markers that do not allow for classification as acute undifferentiated leukaemia, mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia, or leukaemia of a specific lineage. ALAL-NOS includes cases that express T-lineage markers such as CD5 and CD7 but without surface or cytoplasmic CD3, along with myeloid-associated antigens such as CD33 and CD13 (but without myeloperoxidase), and/or CD19 as a B-lineage marker but not other B-lineage markers. Care should be taken not to assign a case as ALAL-NOS on the basis of the expression of certain antigens with limited lineage specificity when such antigens are expressed dimly and/or partially. For example, a leukaemia expressing CD13, CD33, and KIT (CD117) along with CD7 and dim CD19 is more properly regarded as acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) with aberrant antigen expression.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119215,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>See above.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119216,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Full cytogenetic and molecular evaluation is generally necessary before a designation of ALAL-NOS is rendered. Specifically, exclusion of <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1</em> and <em>KMT2A</em> rearrangement is necessary.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119217,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> &ge;&nbsp;20% blasts in bone marrow and/or blood expressing combinations of immunophenotypic lineage markers that do not permit definitive lineage assignments; not fulfilling diagnostic criteria for mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia with defined genetic alterations.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119218,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119219,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 82,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>ALAL-NOS is generally considered to have a poor prognosis, although data on outcomes remain limited {30956966}. The mutation burden may influence outcome {34934076}. Patients are most often treated with AML induction regimens, but anecdotal data suggest response to acute lymphoblastic lymphoma/leukaemia&ndash;directed therapy {23412561; 30956966}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:20:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]